WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.333 --> 00:00:02.835
-Hello, and welcome back
to the captain's quarters.

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:05.972
It's Monday, which means my hair
has had another weekend to grow,

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.940
and while I'm
aiming for the Steff,

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.576
James Spader's iconic haircut
from "Pretty in Pink,"

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:13.145
I might be backing
into James Van Der Beek's

00:00:13.145 --> 00:00:14.580
'do from "Dawson's Creek."

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.416
Now, I've never seen
"Dawson's Creek."

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:18.150
I didn't even know
it was a TV show.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.820
I just assumed it was a meme
that best exemplifies

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.288
how I feel all the time.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:24.190
But my wife is a "Creek" freak

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.526
who is currently rewatching it
on her phone every night in bed,

00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:29.595
and I have
one big observation

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:31.363
based on my introduction
to the show.

00:00:31.363 --> 00:00:34.567
The other characters
say "Dawson" a lot.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.002
Like, even when it's
a two-person scene,

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.704
they start every sentence
with "Dawson," and, look,

00:00:38.704 --> 00:00:40.773
Joey, Jen, I'm not telling you
how to live your life,

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:42.208
but he knows
you're talking to him.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.876
There is no one else
in the room.

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:46.712
Also, Jen, everyone knows you
used to live in New York City.

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:47.914
Let it go.

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:49.883
Did you watch "Dawson's Creek,"
Sea Captain?

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:51.784
-I'm Team Pacey.

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:53.986
-Of course you are.
Now where were we?

00:00:53.986 --> 00:00:55.388
Oh, right, the real world.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.790
As the coronavirus pandemic

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.524
continues to spiral
out of control,

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:01.494
a morally and intellectually
bankrupt Republican Party

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:04.163
is squabbling over
cutting unemployment benefits

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:06.665
for out-of-work Americans
while sending secret police

00:01:06.665 --> 00:01:09.569
to American cities
and whining about cartoons.

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.570
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:13.039
And I am glad it's time
because...

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.540
♪ I don't wanna wait ♪

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.077
♪♪

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:21.380
-We're less than 100 days away
from the presidential election

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:22.915
and more Americans now say

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:24.617
that the country is
on the wrong track

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:27.387
than at any point
in Donald Trump's presidency.

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:29.422
We have got an out-of-control
pandemic,

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.224
the worst unemployment
in nearly a century,

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:33.292
an epidemic of racist
police brutality,

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:35.228
and a looming eviction crisis.

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:37.062
But don't worry.
The Trump administration

00:01:37.062 --> 00:01:40.566
will protect your cartoons
and your toys.

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:43.169
-He is also appalled
by cancel culture,

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:46.138
and cancel culture specifically
as it pertains to cops.

00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:48.641
We saw a few weeks ago
that "Paw Patrol,"

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:51.577
a cartoon show about cops
was canceled,

00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:54.780
the show "Cops" was canceled,
"Live PD" was canceled.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.884
Lego halted the sales of their
Lego City Police Station.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.986
-"Paw Patrol" and Legos
make sense,

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.855
I guess, coming from a guy
who loves rockets,

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:04.423
trucks, and Mr. Potato Dead.

00:02:04.423 --> 00:02:06.059
Anyway, I guess we know now
what Trump does

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:07.593
with all that free time
on his schedule.

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:10.897
"I don't like this
recycling pup, Rocky.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:12.732
I think he's part
of the deep state.

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.634
Kayleigh!

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.902
Kayleigh, send the secret police
to Adventure Bay.

00:02:16.902 --> 00:02:20.039
And get me some more Legos,
Kayleigh.

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:23.009
I stuck one up my nose
to stop the coronavirus.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:26.111
Fauci, by the way, did you get
my email about Legos up the nose

00:02:26.111 --> 00:02:27.714
maybe stopping the virus?

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:29.482
Okay.
I love your thoughts on that.

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:31.417
You're my best friend, Fauci.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.653
You know what I call us?
'Turner and Fauch.'

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.321
I'm going to make t-shirts."

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.623
Anyway, this is where
the Trump administration

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:40.159
and the Republican Party are at,
whining about cartoons and Legos

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.628
while sending secret police
to gas moms and vets

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:46.165
and arguing that slavery
was a, quote, "necessary evil."

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:48.635
A sitting United States Senator
said that.

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:51.004
At least I think Tom Cotton
is a Senator.

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:53.105
He looks like
the Confederate Slender Man.

00:02:53.105 --> 00:02:55.741
Seriously, these guys just keep
coming up with winners.

00:02:55.741 --> 00:02:57.010
I mean, what's next?

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.311
Is Trump going to say
something nice

00:02:58.311 --> 00:02:59.879
about an alleged sex
trafficker and predator

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:02.748
who was arrested by the FBI
at a remote -- oh, yeah, yeah.

00:03:02.748 --> 00:03:04.183
Oh, right.

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:07.287
They really think Americans care
about "Paw Patrol" and Legos.

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:09.054
I guess they figure
if you're out of work

00:03:09.054 --> 00:03:10.290
and quarantining at home

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.759
to avoid the deadly virus
they failed to stop,

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:14.960
you'll need something
to keep you entertained.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.064
"President Trump is working hard
to make sure

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:19.865
that out-of-work Americans
who lost their health insurance

00:03:19.865 --> 00:03:22.101
and are facing eviction
have cartoons

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.136
and Legos
to keep them occupied.

00:03:24.136 --> 00:03:26.739
And in lieu of the $600
unemployment benefit,

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:29.675
we will be sending
every American some Play-Doh

00:03:29.675 --> 00:03:31.177
and an out-of-work
Tamagotchi.

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.911
And I'm sorry?

00:03:32.911 --> 00:03:34.947
The Tamagotchi has died
from the coronavirus."

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:38.217
The craziest part of this though
is that she's wrong.

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:41.353
Neither "Paw Patrol"
nor the Lego City Police Station

00:03:41.353 --> 00:03:42.722
have been canceled.

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:45.958
In fact, "Paw Patrol"
actually had to tweet

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:48.527
a clarification saying,
"No need to worry.

00:03:48.527 --> 00:03:51.831
'Paw Patrol' is not canceled."
And that's great.

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:54.667
But, you know, they could also
stand to be defunded a little.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.803
I mean, that's an awful lot
of tactical gear for a town

00:03:57.803 --> 00:03:59.638
where the worst thing that ever
happens is a missing chicken.

00:03:59.638 --> 00:04:02.374
So the Trump administration
got fact-checked

00:04:02.374 --> 00:04:03.576
by a children's cartoon.

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:05.311
And at this point,
it's not long before

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.313
Arthur shows up to a protest
with a sign

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:08.648
that says "[Bleep] Trump."

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:10.182
-Seth, that reminds me,

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:13.352
what's a sea captain's
favorite animal?

00:04:13.352 --> 00:04:15.888
-Oh, I don't know, what is a sea
captain's favorite animal?

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:17.957
-An arrrr-dvark!

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:20.226
-Sea Captain!
-Ha, ha, ha!

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:21.793
Sorry.
-So what was I talking about?

00:04:21.793 --> 00:04:23.529
Oh, right.
Children's cartoons.

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:26.232
The point is this is what your
government was talking about

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:28.700
as a federal moratorium
on evictions

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.836
and a $600
unemployment benefit

00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:34.006
keeping millions of Americans
afloat both expired.

00:04:34.006 --> 00:04:36.942
And rather than rushing
with extreme urgency

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:38.344
to extend both programs,

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:41.213
or, heaven forbid,
make them permanent,

00:04:41.213 --> 00:04:42.882
Republicans chose
instead to dawdle

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:45.317
as they bickered over ways
to make the unemployment program

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:48.053
both less generous
and more complicated.

00:04:48.053 --> 00:04:49.789
Mitch McConnell said
a new stimulus deal

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:50.956
could take a few weeks.

00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:53.225
Why?
Just extend it now.

00:04:53.225 --> 00:04:55.828
Jobless claims went up
for the first time since March,

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:58.530
four million Americans who do
have jobs have seen a pay cut,

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:01.801
12 million are facing eviction
as the moratorium expires.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:04.937
In Oklahoma, more than 60%
of unemployment applications

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:06.438
haven't even been processed,

00:05:06.438 --> 00:05:08.841
with hundreds of people
sleeping in their cars

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:11.377
or camping outside
Oklahoma's unemployment offices.

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:13.712
And in Ohio, the city
of Columbus

00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:15.381
has turned part of
its convention center

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:16.649
into an evictions court.

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:17.984
Well, you got to give it
to Trump,

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:19.452
he finally filled an arena.

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:21.253
Oh, and on top of that,
nurses are wearing gowns

00:05:21.253 --> 00:05:23.122
without openings for hands
and secret police

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:25.924
are marching through the streets
of Portland tear-gassing vets

00:05:25.924 --> 00:05:28.360
and moms while protesters
play the Imperial March

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:29.828
from "Star Wars."

00:05:29.828 --> 00:05:32.498
[ Imperial March plays ]
[ Firing ]

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:33.832
[ Bursts ]

00:05:33.832 --> 00:05:38.304
[ Firing continues ]
♪♪

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:39.438
That's a pretty great troll.

00:05:39.438 --> 00:05:41.307
Of course, if George Lucas
was involved,

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:43.208
he'd probably add
in some unnecessary CGI

00:05:43.208 --> 00:05:45.077
and a gratuitous pod race.

00:05:45.077 --> 00:05:48.180
So what was the president doing
while the nation was crumbling?

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:49.715
You guessed it.

00:05:49.715 --> 00:05:52.684
He was playing golf and smiling
for photos with Brett Favre.

00:05:52.684 --> 00:05:54.086
Cheeseheads always loved Favre,

00:05:54.086 --> 00:05:56.389
so it makes sense that
ol' cheese brain would, too.

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:57.857
Also, what's going on here, man?

00:05:57.857 --> 00:06:00.459
He looks like he just crawled
out of a vat at Ace Chemicals.

00:06:00.459 --> 00:06:01.827
This is how a dog smiles

00:06:01.827 --> 00:06:03.429
when they have their head
out the window.

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:05.998
That's the face you make
when you're trying to hold in

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:07.633
a fart at a funeral.

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:10.069
Not that I think Trump would
bother trying to hold it in.

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:11.737
"Whoa, whoo!

00:06:11.737 --> 00:06:14.574
Well, boy, if that doesn't wake
him up, he's definitely dead."

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:16.174
Although in fairness,
it's probably better

00:06:16.174 --> 00:06:18.610
when Trump's golfing
because then he's too busy

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:21.214
to whine about cartoons
and Legos and statues.

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:24.116
This bottom-of-the-barrel
culture war bull [bleep]

00:06:24.116 --> 00:06:25.484
is the result
of a political movement

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:27.520
that is intellectually barren
and morally bankrupt.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:30.622
They have nothing to run on,
no policies to champion,

00:06:30.622 --> 00:06:32.291
no achievements to tout.

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:34.093
So they think they
can get voters

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:35.828
to care about statues
and cartoons.

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:37.229
It's all they have left,

00:06:37.229 --> 00:06:40.032
and that's because Americans
know Trump has failed.

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:41.567
It's clear in poll after poll.

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:43.669
All you have do is look at one
of the dozens

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:45.438
of other large
developed countries

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:47.339
that have successfully
suppressed their outbreaks

00:06:47.339 --> 00:06:49.608
while keeping their economies
largely intact.

00:06:49.608 --> 00:06:51.977
South Korea had its first case
on the same day as ours

00:06:51.977 --> 00:06:53.946
and rapidly
contained their outbreak.

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:57.016
The entirety of the EU,
with a much larger population,

00:06:57.016 --> 00:07:00.853
has an average of just 81 deaths
per day while we're at 1,000.

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:02.521
Americans can't even go
to Canada or Europe,

00:07:02.521 --> 00:07:04.390
which means for the first time
this century,

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.825
no one will take a picture
trying to make it look like

00:07:06.825 --> 00:07:09.628
they're holding up
the Leaning Tower of Pisa.

00:07:09.628 --> 00:07:12.364
Americans can plainly see
that things are not just bad,

00:07:12.364 --> 00:07:13.766
but getting worse while
the rest of the world

00:07:13.766 --> 00:07:16.602
watches us with a combination
of pity and horror

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:19.571
and probably a little less
surprise than we think.

00:07:19.571 --> 00:07:20.806
[ French accent ]
"It is so sad

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:22.508
what is happening
to your country."

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:24.143
[ Normal voice ] "I know,
it's shocking, right?"

00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:25.611
[ French accent ]
"Yeah, eh, shocking?

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:27.846
I would not use this word.

00:07:27.846 --> 00:07:30.816
It is -- how do you say?

00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:32.351
To be expected."

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:34.787
We've seen our outbreak spiral
out of control

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:37.656
in a way that's even worse
than the initial peak in April.

00:07:37.656 --> 00:07:40.125
The White House
National Security Advisor

00:07:40.125 --> 00:07:41.360
just tested positive.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:43.229
Major League Baseball
has an outbreak

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:45.464
just days
after starting its season.

00:07:45.464 --> 00:07:47.834
We're nearing a national peak
in hospitalizations.

00:07:47.834 --> 00:07:51.404
We recorded 1,000 new deaths
a day for four straight days.

00:07:51.404 --> 00:07:53.606
And labs across the country
are once again

00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:56.775
facing long delays in testing
thanks to supply shortages.

00:07:56.775 --> 00:07:58.444
Or, as one public
health official put it,

00:07:58.444 --> 00:08:00.079
"It's like 'Groundhog Day.'

00:08:00.079 --> 00:08:02.281
I feel like I've lived this day
four or five months ago."

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:03.649
Except in "Groundhog Day,"

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:04.850
Bill Murray learned
to play the piano

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:06.351
and became a better person.

00:08:06.351 --> 00:08:08.054
All I've learned is that doing
a late night show in your attic

00:08:08.054 --> 00:08:09.955
is kind of like
making a video will,

00:08:09.955 --> 00:08:12.458
except I am not of sound mind.

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:14.459
-Sure you are.

00:08:14.459 --> 00:08:16.328
-Thank you, talking
yard sale painting.

00:08:16.328 --> 00:08:18.830
Quarantine has lasted so long,
I've come full circle

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:20.398
and started watching
"Tiger King" again.

00:08:20.398 --> 00:08:21.700
Gonna give Joe Exotic

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:22.935
one more chance
to convince me I'm wrong.

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:24.636
If you asked me what day
it is right now,

00:08:24.636 --> 00:08:27.373
I'd say
Januaugustober 67th.

00:08:27.373 --> 00:08:30.209
The only concrete day
I can picture

00:08:30.209 --> 00:08:31.477
is the first day of school,

00:08:31.477 --> 00:08:32.778
and I'm terrified
it's not going to happen

00:08:32.778 --> 00:08:34.112
because instead of making a plan

00:08:34.112 --> 00:08:36.215
on how to get kids
and teachers back safely,

00:08:36.215 --> 00:08:39.117
we prioritized opening
a Crunch Fitness in Gainesville.

00:08:39.117 --> 00:08:41.320
I hope you fellas got
swole enough

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:43.822
to make up for the fact that
my kids can't count past seven.

00:08:43.822 --> 00:08:46.758
Seriously, we should have had
testing figured out months ago.

00:08:46.758 --> 00:08:48.928
That was the whole point
of flattening the curve,

00:08:48.928 --> 00:08:51.430
to buy time
for our policymakers

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:53.866
to get a system of testing,
tracing, and isolation in place

00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:55.701
so we could contain
future outbreaks.

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:56.935
Remember that?

00:08:56.935 --> 00:08:58.537
When we all kept saying
"flatten the curve"?

00:08:58.537 --> 00:09:00.172
Back when Dr. Fauci

00:09:00.172 --> 00:09:02.574
was the one briefing the nation
at press conferences

00:09:02.574 --> 00:09:05.277
instead of chucking a ball
like your grandpa used to?

00:09:05.277 --> 00:09:06.712
"I'll go get it, Grandpa."

00:09:06.712 --> 00:09:09.414
"Look both ways when you
cross the street."

00:09:09.414 --> 00:09:10.916
And yet, the President
and the GOP

00:09:10.916 --> 00:09:12.885
have shown zero interest
in fixing the problem.

00:09:12.885 --> 00:09:14.520
In fact, Trump is so deeply

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:16.455
invested in his own
political fortunes

00:09:16.455 --> 00:09:18.824
and so profoundly
detached from reality,

00:09:18.824 --> 00:09:20.492
that he still thinks
it would be better

00:09:20.492 --> 00:09:23.261
if we stop testing altogether
and just let the virus

00:09:23.261 --> 00:09:25.698
rip through the country
sickening people undetected.

00:09:25.698 --> 00:09:27.866
-I personally think
it's overrated,

00:09:27.866 --> 00:09:29.735
but I am totally willing
to keep doing it.

00:09:29.735 --> 00:09:31.470
I'm okay with it
if they want to do it,

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:35.307
but again, it makes us look bad.

00:09:35.307 --> 00:09:36.609
But think of it.

00:09:36.609 --> 00:09:39.077
If instead of 50 million
we did 25 million,

00:09:39.077 --> 00:09:40.479
we don't have
the number of cases.

00:09:40.479 --> 00:09:41.847
The cases would be down.

00:09:41.847 --> 00:09:43.415
Here would be
the normally headline.

